# Test-only relaxations on top of the project root .clang-tidy.
#
# Tests construct deliberate edge cases (oversize bodies, magic
# constants, mismatched argument labels for clarity) and the costs of
# being strict here are visible: every churn-grade nit blocks the push
# gate and forces a follow-up commit. Production code stays under the
# full check set; we only loosen the inputs to test_host/.
#
# `InheritParentConfig: true` keeps every check from the root
# `.clang-tidy` enabled — we only subtract the two checks that have
# repeatedly fired on test files without flagging real bugs:
#
#   bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result
#     Hit by `16U * 1024U` literals passed to size_t parameters; the
#     widening is intentional and the constants are obvious.
#
#   bugprone-argument-comment
#     Tests use shorter `/*sats=*/` style comments for readability;
#     the parameter-name match against the production header isn't
#     load-bearing in test code.

InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  -bugprone-argument-comment
